{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1qdR41THck8D7pxj8cq", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not signing off. I found two problems and reproduced each more than once, but the developer could not reproduce either from my steps. I also could not cover the Antiandrogen dose lookup across several slots.\n\n**Reported (both answered \"could not reproduce\"):**\n1. **Preparation form amounts are not carried over.** With Tablet strength set to 2 mg, switching to Patch left \"Total amount in patch (mg)\" empty, and switching to Injection left \"Vial strength (mg)\" empty. The value only came back when I switched to Tablet again, so it is kept per form, not carried over. I reproduced this three times, using a preset and typed values.\n2. **Group editor does not re-sort times after an edit.** In Group 1, changing 6:58 AM to 11:58 AM left the row first, so the list read \"6:58 AM → 11:58 AM\", then \"8:00 AM → 10:00 AM\", then \"9:58 PM\". Saving and reopening sorts it correctly. I reproduced this twice.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- Add medicine: all four categories and the forms switch without errors. Cancel discards the sheet. Medicines save and show correctly.\n- Group creation: times sort as added (12:00 AM, 6:58 AM, 9:58 PM). Save and Plan show the same times.\n- Home: the Antiandrogen card shows Spironolactone \"Oral · 50 mg\", which matches the Plan slots. Today's slot counts agree between Home and Plan. The card status changes correctly after midnight. Rotating to landscape and back loses nothing.\n- Group editor: Discard reverts unsaved changes. Weekly shows the day chips and time.\n\n**Not covered:** Gel and Patch save flows, the Estradiol chart window controls, Journal and Settings, and archiving. I could not give two slots different doses for the same antiandrogen, so the \"dose looked up across all slots\" change is untested.\n\n**Data I created on the device** (remove if the device is reused):\n- Estradiol valerate, Tablet, 5 mg\n- Spironolactone, Tablet, 50 mg (Antiandrogen)\n- Group 1: Estradiol valerate, starts Nov 14, times 6:58 AM, 8:00 AM, 9:58 PM\n- Group 2: Spironolactone, starts Nov 13, times 12:00 AM and 9:59 PM\n\nI did not log any doses."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2326, "cache_read_input_tokens": 298716, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2326}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d692458a-d2bc-41e1-8985-78180438e3be", "uuid": "ebd7ee12-98cc-4656-9a1e-dc60e3508fd9", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:02:10.837Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1qdQkQiPkPuoEwh18QE"}
